r MLP (1024 -> 512 -> 256 -> 1) with BatchNorm and Dropout (0.3). This architectural deepening directly targets the saturated performance by providing more parameters to model fine-grained texture variations while attention guides focus on relevant regions.", "training_evaluation": "Switch the loss to Focal Loss with label smoothing (alpha=0.75, gamma=2.0, label_smoothing=0.05) to handle class imbalance and improve calibration. Replace the CosineAnnealingLR with OneCycleLR (max_lr=1e-3 for head, 5e-5 for backbone) to accelerate convergence and reduce overfitting. Enable mixed precision training with gradient clipping (max_norm=1.0). For final predictions, apply test-time augmentation (horizontal flip) averaging to both validation and test inference to boost robustness and AUC. Keep the same train/val split (random_state=42) and evaluation metric for fair comparison."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
